@@ -33,6 +33,16 @@ The API is intentionally not an automation or dashboard-management API.
 Connecting a Rivian account, changing vehicle settings, creating dashboards,
 and every administrative operation require a signed-in browser session.
 
+`GET /v1/vehicles/{id}/charging-schedule/upstream` is a session-only,
+owner/manager route for attended Rivian control experiments. It reads the
+complete charging-schedule array directly from Rivian and returns an
+`observed_at` timestamp. It never writes the local schedule row and sends
+`Cache-Control: no-store`; an omitted provider vehicle or schedule list is an
+error rather than an empty schedule. The response may include saved-location
+latitude and longitude; keep any retained response or recovery snapshot in
+restricted storage, and redact coordinates, VINs, account identifiers, and
+tokens from worksheets and logs. Integration keys are denied.
+
 Chart management follows the same session-only boundary. The signed-in web app
 uses `/v1/charts`, `/v1/charts/effective`, `/v1/chart-sources`, and the chart
 clone, placement, enabled, reset, and admin restore routes. Integration keys do
